# Engagement mandate — {{CLIENT_NAME}}

**What was agreed before you landed.** Someone sold this work, to someone, on some basis, and probably promised something. That is the boundary every later scope decision is judged against — so it is written down here rather than recalled.

The runbook is clear that the assessment is what "converts an open-ended AI conversation into a bounded piece of work with a deliverable." This file is that boundary. Without it, `scope-changes.md` adjudicates against a sentence somebody typed from memory on day one.

**Fill this before the first client meeting, not after.** If you cannot, that is itself the finding, and it belongs in `02-Workflow/open-questions.md` with a name against it.

