`Primary document` names the thing, and `mandate.documents` below says where it lives. Do not paste contract text into this file.

## Outcomes promised

Everything said during the sale that the client could reasonably expect us to deliver. **An unmeasurable promise is the one that resurfaces at the readout**, phrased as though it had always been precise.

<!-- table:mandate.promised role=register id=Id -->

| Id | Promise | Made to | Where stated | Measurable? | Measured by |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|

`Measurable?` is `yes` or `no`, and `no` is a legitimate and common answer. Record it as `no` and raise a `Q-` rather than inventing a metric nobody agreed to.

## The boundary

<!-- table:mandate.boundary role=register id=Item -->

| Item | In / out / silent | Where stated | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|

**`silent` is the interesting value.** In and out were both negotiated; silent is everything nobody discussed, and that is where scope creep enters — as a small helpful addition during a working session, not as a change request. A two-value column hides exactly the rows you need.

